; horner-wide-fp64 - a degree-299 Horner whose coefficients arrive per
; run, past the 256 a byte of imm reaches
;
; docs/SEQUENCER.md revision 3, R7: under `kx` a constant index is NINE
; bits - a byte of `imm` and its ninth in imm[30:28], one per operand -
; so the bank holds 512 and this program addresses 300 of them. The
; source says nothing about that: the assembler picks the plain form
; for an index below sixteen, the indexed form from sixteen, and sets
; the ninth bit from 256. `cft-asm -i` names KX9 among the features the
; image needs, and `cft_program_load` refuses the image on a device
; whose CAPS[7] is clear rather than letting an eight-bit operand mux
; address the wrong constant.
;
; It is also a BANK_EXT program (revision 2's R3), so the image carries
; no constant section at all: 2448 bytes of pure schedule, and the
; three hundred coefficients arrive per run in
; horner-wide-fp64.recip.bank - C[k] = (-1)^k / (k+1), each the
; library's own correctly-rounded quotient rather than a decimal
; somebody typed.
;
; The first line is a `copysign` of C0 with itself, which is an exact
; bit copy for every operand including the zeroes and the infinities -
; the usual `fma acc, zero, x, C0` would be a NaN at x = inf, and a
; move that is only correct for the inputs a check happens to use is
; not a move.

.format   fp64
.deposits 1
.bank     external

